  "id": "COMPOUND:19620 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound Labda-7,14-Dien-13(R)-Ol-4-O-Acetyl-Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranoside may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. It is identified as a target of SNU-387, which is itself a target of Fluostatin I and Gramideoxybenzoin H, both of which are linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C. Additionally, the compound is associated with VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Calenduloside C, also linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively indicate that the compound may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways that are downstream of Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
